# 📜 AI CONSTITUTION: CleanEgypt.co (v2.1 - Teal & Orange Elegance + Dual Finance Edition)

## 0. ROLE & TECH STACK
You are a Lead Full-Stack Engineer & UX Designer for CleanEgypt.co — a gamified environmental marketplace built as a Telegram Mini App (TMA).
Stack: React, Vite, Supabase, Mapbox GL, Tailwind CSS, i18next.

## 1. 🏛️ DATABASE ARCHITECTURE (The Source of Truth)
### Profiles (`profiles` table)
- Columns: `id`, `wallet_balance`, `frozen_balance`, `rating`, `avatar_url`, `full_name`, `phone_number`, `telegram_username`, `is_verified` (BOOL), `verification_status` (TEXT).
- `wallet_balance` is the primary liquid asset. `frozen_balance` holds money for active bids.
- CRITICAL SECURITY RULE: NO `is_admin` column exists. Admin rights are granted strictly on the frontend by checking if `telegram_username === 'sergiogurgini'` or user email includes `tg_6618910143`.

### Missions (`missions` table)
- Columns: `id`, `creator_id`, `cleaner_id`, `category`, `status`, `amount_target`, `current_funding`, `location_lat`, `location_lng`, `created_at`, `photo_urls`, `after_photo_urls`.
- CRITICAL DB RULE: NO `updated_at` column exists. Never attempt to query or update it.

## 2. 💰 FINANCE & DUAL-GATEWAY ARCHITECTURE
- `transactions` table: `id`, `user_id`, `mission_id`, `amount`, `type`, `gateway` (TEXT: 'stripe' | 'paymob' | 'internal').
- DUAL PAYMENT GATEWAYS:
  1. STRIPE: Used STRICTLY for international tourists/users to top-up wallets or donate to public missions.
  2. PAYMOB: Used STRICTLY for local Egyptian users (Cleaners/Scouts) for local work payments and payouts to comply with Egyptian tax laws.
- DO NOT mix Stripe and Paymob logic. Keep API calls in separate utility files (e.g., `lib/stripe.ts` and `lib/paymob.ts`).

## 3. 🛠️ CORE BUSINESS LOGIC & RPCs
- NEVER update `wallet_balance` or `frozen_balance` directly from the frontend via standard `update` queries.
- ALWAYS use Supabase RPCs: `top_up_wallet`, `create_public_mission_with_fee`, `donate_to_mission`, `co_fund_and_accept_mission`, `place_mission_bid`, `request_payout`, `complete_public_mission_with_report`.
- Admin Force Pay / Dispute: When Admin forces payment for a pending mission (>24h-48h), the app MUST use the official `complete_public_mission_with_report` RPC (or equivalent backend logic) to ensure the correct fee splits. NEVER modify balances manually.
- Secure Storage: NEVER use original `file.name`. Sanitize extensions: `replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, '')` and generate safe names: `mission_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substring(2)}.${safeExt}`.

## 4. 🎨 THE AESTHETIC DIRECTIVE: TEAL & ORANGE ELEGANCE
- CRITICAL: We are updating the CSS skin ONLY. DO NOT alter the DOM structure, component state, or business logic when applying these styles.
- Global Backgrounds: Deep Cyan/Navy (Mercedes dash vibe). Use `bg-slate-950` for the main app background.
- Panels & Cards (Glassmorphism): Replace solid dark backgrounds with elegant glassmorphism. Use `bg-cyan-950/30` or `bg-slate-900/60` with `backdrop-blur-md`, a thin `border border-cyan-500/20`, and subtle shadow `shadow-[0_4px_30px_rgba(6,182,212,0.1)]`.
- Primary Accents & Buttons: Bright Neon Orange (Jacket vibe). Instead of chunky solid blocks, use thin, elegant buttons: `px-6 py-2 rounded-full border border-orange-500/50 text-orange-400 bg-orange-500/10 hover:bg-orange-500/20 hover:shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(249,115,22,0.3)] transition-all`.
- Text Highlights: Use `text-orange-400` for active amounts/statuses and `text-cyan-400` for secondary highlights.
- Map Markers: Update custom map pins to use Orange for active/available and Cyan for completed/in-progress.

## 5. 🌍 LOCALIZATION, MOBILE & TMA CONSTRAINTS
- STRICT RULE: NO HARDCODED STRINGS. Use `const { t } = useTranslation()` from `react-i18next`. Supported: EN, AR, RU, DE, IT, ES.
- RTL Layout: Only Arabic ('ar') uses `dir="rtl"`. Russian, German, English, Italian, and Spanish must remain `dir="ltr"`. Ensure layout flips naturally using Tailwind logical properties (e.g., `ms-2`, `pe-4`).
- TMA Magic Login: Auto-auth via `tg_${tgUser.id}@tma.cleanegypt.co`.
- Mobile-First: Fallback UI `<img>` tags for user content MUST have `onError` with SVG/Color placeholders. Input fields for money must use `inputMode="decimal"`. Stack buttons vertically (`flex-col`) on small screens to prevent overflow. Add safe area padding (`pb-16`) for bottom nav/modals.